---
import BaseLayout from '../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import DeploymentStatusMeta from '../../../../components/jurisdictions/DeploymentStatusMeta.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="DeKalb County Surveillance | NoRec.US"
  description="Documented surveillance technology used by DeKalb-area agencies, including Genetec and Flock ALPR, Axon Body 4 and Fleet 3, Axon Fusus licensing, drones, and camera-registration programs."
  active="surveillance"
>
<main class="page_shell">
  <nav class="jurisdiction_breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="/illinois/">Illinois</a><span>→</span><strong>Dekalb County</strong>
  </nav>
  <header class="article_header">
    <p class="eyebrow">LOCAL SURVEILLANCE · DEKALB COUNTY, ILLINOIS</p>
    <h1>DeKalb County</h1>
    <p class="article_deck">DeKalb's public records provide unusually detailed documentation of ALPR, body-camera, in-car video, real-time vehicle systems, drone policy, and networked evidence software.</p>
  </header>
<section>
  <p class="eyebrow">MUNICIPALITIES</p>
  <h2>City and village research</h2>
  <div class="jurisdiction_cards">
    <a href="/illinois/counties/dekalb/cities/dekalb/"><strong>DeKalb</strong><span>Municipal dossier available</span></a>
  </div>
  <p class="map_note">Additional municipalities can be added as records are contributed. An unlisted municipality should not be interpreted as having no surveillance technology.</p>
</section>


  

  

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">CURRENT ALPR CONTRACT</p>
    <h2>DeKalb Police has a 2026–2027 Flock service agreement.</h2>
    <div class="finding_grid">
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span>
        <DeploymentStatusMeta evidenceStatus="documented" operationalStatus="active" verifiedAsOf="2026-09-18" sourceAsOf="2026-06-22" owner="DeKalb Police Department" />
        <h3>Two-year Flock ALPR service contract</h3>
        <p>Resolution 2026-059, approved June 22, 2026, authorizes a Flock Safety contract for Police Department automatic-license-plate-reader service for a two-year 2026–2027 term, not to exceed $27,500.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">HISTORICAL BASELINE</span>
        <h3>2021 Genetec purchase remains a separate dated record</h3>
        <p>DeKalb's 2021 resolution documented 12 Genetec LPRs. The newer Flock contract does not, by itself, establish whether every Genetec reader was removed, retained, or integrated, so NoRec does not combine the two procurements into a current device total.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">DRONES</p>
    <h2>County and municipal UAS programs</h2>
    <div class="finding_grid">
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span>
        <h3>DeKalb County Sheriff: three drones</h3>
        <p>The SFY 2024 statewide drone report lists three Sheriff's Office drones and seven flights, including missing-person searches, fire assessment, crash documentation, and a suicidal-subject response.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span>
        <h3>DeKalb Police: one drone</h3>
        <p>The same statewide report lists DeKalb Police as owning one drone. The city's current UAS policy was revised in March 2026.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED POLICY</span>
        <h3>Sheriff UAS safeguards</h3>
        <p>The Sheriff's published UAS policy addresses statutory restrictions, facial-recognition use, prohibited random surveillance, weaponization, retention, annual reporting, and disclosure.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED POLICY</span>
        <h3>City UAS safeguards</h3>
        <p>DeKalb Police policy 407.12 references the Freedom from Drone Surveillance Act, the Drones as First Responders Act, privacy rights, FAA requirements, and statutory exclusions for protected demonstrations from defined event categories.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">PRIMARY SOURCES</p>
    <ul class="provider_source_list">
      <li><a href="https://www.cityofdekalb.com/DocumentCenter/View/13234/Res-2021-093-Passed-101121-Genetec-LPR">Resolution 2021-093 — 12 Genetec LPRs</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.cityofdekalb.com/1599/2026-Resolutions">2026 resolutions — Flock Safety ALPR contract</a></li>
